What is the output of the following program where private method has identical signature in subclass?
```java
class SuperSecretBase {
    public void test() {
        secret();
    }
    private void secret() {
        System.out.print("BaseSecret ");
    }
}
class SubSecretDerived extends SuperSecretBase {
    private void secret() {
        System.out.print("DerivedSecret ");
    }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SuperSecretBase ssb = new SubSecretDerived();
        ssb.test();
    }
}
```

What is the output of the following polymorphic method invocation on array elements?
```java
class ShapeDrawer {
    void draw() { System.out.print("Shape "); }
}
class CircleDrawer extends ShapeDrawer {
    @Override
    void draw() { System.out.print("Circle "); }
}
class SquareDrawer extends ShapeDrawer {
    @Override
    void draw() { System.out.print("Square "); }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        ShapeDrawer[] drawers = { new CircleDrawer(), new SquareDrawer() };
        for (ShapeDrawer d : drawers) {
            d.draw();
        }
    }
}
```

What is the output of the following constructor call to overridable method?
```java
class ParentDevice {
    ParentDevice() {
        setup();
    }
    void setup() {
        System.out.print("ParentSetup ");
    }
}
class ChildDevice extends ParentDevice {
    int code = 99;
    @Override
    void setup() {
        System.out.print("Child:" + code + " ");
    }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        new ChildDevice();
    }
}
```

What is the output of the following field hiding vs method overriding combination?
```java
class VehicleUnit {
    int speed = 50;
    int getSpeed() { return speed; }
}
class RaceCarUnit extends VehicleUnit {
    int speed = 150;
    @Override
    int getSpeed() { return speed; }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        VehicleUnit vu = new RaceCarUnit();
        System.out.println(vu.speed + ":" + vu.getSpeed());
    }
}
```
